{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update","id":974244,"title":"Dual Kith Update","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T22:37:10-07:00","id":974244,"title":"Dual Kith Update","content":"I've had a few questions about Dual Kith in 2E. Here's what we're looking at now, different from the original copy I shared:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dual Kith \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not change.<br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> When taking this Merit, choose one kith as your primary kith. When calculating your kith advantage, your character\u2019s effective Wyrd has one fewer dot, to a minimum of one. The secondary kith\u2019s Wyrd is considered two dots fewer, to a minimum of one as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:53:16-07:00","id":974248,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised it's only two dots... and now I have to completely restructure my court's mantles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:01:33-07:00","id":974251,"title":"","content":"Cool, nice idea !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:05:47-07:00","id":974253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974248#post974248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised it's only two dots... and now I have to completely restructure my court's mantles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to make it a little more accessible, since I added that drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:10:46-07:00","id":974254,"title":"","content":"Cool. I didn't have any problem with the older version, but if this helps keep Dual Kith a thing, I'm cool with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:13:39-07:00","id":974255,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty cheap, but I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:41:09-07:00","id":974264,"title":"","content":"I think it's a nice balance of the issues with the original version with keeping the spirit of the idea alive.<br /> <br /> The weakness is going to be variable, since many of the preview Kiths don't use Wyrd, but for those where Wyrd matters, this is a significant choice of versatility over power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:57:56-07:00","id":974268,"title":"","content":"Question: How does Potent Kith interact with this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:14:55-07:00","id":974273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974264#post974264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a nice balance of the issues with the original version with keeping the spirit of the idea alive.<br /> <br /> The weakness is going to be variable, since many of the preview Kiths don't use Wyrd, but for those where Wyrd matters, this is a significant choice of versatility over power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to see to it that all use it at least in some capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:16:07-07:00","id":974274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974268#post974268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: How does Potent Kith interact with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll add to your main kith, but not your secondary one. I'll note that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:42:45-07:00","id":974280,"title":"","content":"Well... I didn't imagine it would be quite that elegant of a solution, but consider all my concerns expressed in the old thread about 2e Dual Kiths officially addressed. You amaze yet again good sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:54:14-07:00","id":974281,"title":"","content":"Have to say, this is an impressively useful middle ground. I'm always a bit leery of auto-grab merits beyond status or resources and once my players found it, they were pretty much always dual-kithed. This being cheaper, but having a solid draw back makes it a much more interesting merit in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":".  Spelling 09-22-2016, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T01:03:26-07:00","id":974286,"title":"","content":"So the merit is exchanging effectiveness against versatility? I'm not sure about this. Two weak abilities are rarely worth a single strong one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T03:19:45-07:00","id":974318,"title":"","content":"The merit is very well balanced, and its cheapness gives more space for other merits. The new Seeming quest is a good template for a extra kith quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-22-2016, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:51:24-07:00","id":974436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974286#post974286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the merit is exchanging effectiveness against versatility? I'm not sure about this. Two weak abilities are rarely worth a single strong one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call the effective Wyrd reduction two &quot;weak&quot; abilities. The preview Kiths so far (even just looking at the ones with Wyrd in their calculations since the others are getting tweaked) are totally worth having at Wyrd 1; frequently because Kiths offer a few bonuses only one of which relies on Wyrd.<br /> <br /> They're going to be weaker than if you stick single Kith, but that doesn't make them weak in comparison to everything else.<br /> <br /> Which is addressing something a lot of us had problems with in 1e and 2e continuing along the same path in the previews: Dual Kith just got you double the powers for no drawback besides cost, and the cost was generally always less than the potency of the Merit to keep it accessible to people that wanted it for aesthetic reasons over mechanical ones.<br /> <br /> Now Dual Kith is a choice that you'll want to consider rather than a no-brainer Merit you're going to take unless there's a compelling reason you can't spare those Merit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:11:35-07:00","id":974487,"title":"","content":"Nice. I guess the only issue I have is the framing of one Kith being &quot;primary&quot; over the other, but a -1 to both likely doesn't go far enough, and a -2 is likely too far. Half progression on both is likely also crippling. Choosing how to allot your Wyrd-based Kith abilities/effects also doesn't seem feasible. This is probably as good as it can be, baring further testing leading to different outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:01:26-07:00","id":974649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974436#post974436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't call the effective Wyrd reduction two &quot;weak&quot; abilities. The preview Kiths so far (even just looking at the ones with Wyrd in their calculations since the others are getting tweaked) are totally worth having at Wyrd 1; frequently because Kiths offer a few bonuses only one of which relies on Wyrd.<br /> <br /> They're going to be weaker than if you stick single Kith, but that doesn't make them weak in comparison to everything else.<br /> <br /> Which is addressing something a lot of us had problems with in 1e and 2e continuing along the same path in the previews: Dual Kith just got you double the powers for no drawback besides cost, and the cost was generally always less than the potency of the Merit to keep it accessible to people that wanted it for aesthetic reasons over mechanical ones.<br /> <br /> Now Dual Kith is a choice that you'll want to consider rather than a no-brainer Merit you're going to take unless there's a compelling reason you can't spare those Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I don't understand. Dual Kith is a merit. Something you pay for having. Why should it have a drawback? A character with a fighting merit is deadlier than a character without one, with no drawback and nobody complain about that.<br /> <br /> I'd get if only the second kith had reduced benefits, but weakening the 1st one too will basically force you to buy another merit just to compensate the penalty, or play the CofD version D&amp;D 3e 'master of none' Bard, given that at least at low Wyrd it is kinda brutal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:11:19-07:00","id":974654,"title":"","content":"I think the point was to make the merit not be seen as a must have, now its just good and its not the first merit to have a draw back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T14:13:53-07:00","id":974655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974649#post974649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I don't understand. Dual Kith is a merit. Something you pay for having. Why should it have a drawback? A character with a fighting merit is deadlier than a character without one, with no drawback and nobody complain about that.<br /> <br /> I'd get if only the second kith had reduced benefits, but weakening the 1st one too will basically force you to buy another merit just to compensate the penalty, or play the CofD version D&amp;D 3e 'master of none' Bard, given that at least at low Wyrd it is kinda brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a knock-down, drag-out fight for... Pretty much since the original Dual-Kith Merit came out in Rites of Spring. Honestly, while I agree with you that it's fine with the cost being the only drawback, I'm just happy that the Merit is still going to appear in 2e, and that its drawback isn't prohibitively harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:53:32-07:00","id":974787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974649#post974649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I don't understand. Dual Kith is a merit. Something you pay for having. Why should it have a drawback? A character with a fighting merit is deadlier than a character without one, with no drawback and nobody complain about that.<br /> <br /> I'd get if only the second kith had reduced benefits, but weakening the 1st one too will basically force you to buy another merit just to compensate the penalty, or play the CofD version D&amp;D 3e 'master of none' Bard, given that at least at low Wyrd it is kinda brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters are more than their Kith blessings. Their normal blessing is just one of a myriad of abilities they possess, and a pretty minor one all things considered. This is nothing like a 3e Bard. It'd be more like a Fighter Feat that lets her choose to take -1 to her base attack bonus in order to access sneak attack from the Thief abilities, but it does one fewer d6 in sneak attack damage.<br /> <br /> A lot of Merits have drawbacks. Especially supernatural Merits. If the first Kith went without modification, there'd still be literally no argument for NOT doing Dual Kith. This gives a negligible but very present incentive for not every character being Dual Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 09-22-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:56:29-07:00","id":974810,"title":"","content":"I'm strongly in favor of this change, makes it feel like something I'd want often but not always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:02:10-07:00","id":974815,"title":"","content":"Heh. This scales weirdly at low Wyrd (being the floor of 1 Wyrd means that a 1 Wyrd changeling has two full power Kiths), but the drawback bites as they go up in power.<br /> <br /> Still, seems like a sensible compromise anyway. And ridiculously easy to houserule if you don't like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:55:09-07:00","id":974828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974274#post974274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'll add to your main kith, but not your secondary one. I'll note that.</div> </div> </div> </div>say would it be fair to take Potent Kith again for the second Kith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:56:20-07:00","id":974830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974828#post974828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> say would it be fair to take Potent Kith again for the second Kith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. So. I think this is one of those places where I'm not going to make it explicit. I would probably say no in my games. But, if you want to do it in your games, that's cool. I don't feel like it's important enough to need a hard rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:32:17-07:00","id":974845,"title":"","content":"On the whole &quot;why have drawbacks&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> The basic design logic is pretty simple. A drawback lets you reduce the cost of a Merit so that it remains accessible. This is important for Merits that have a lot of flavor, but also a lot of potency in concept. If you valued Dual Kith at what it can be effectively worth at the high-mid level of optimization, it could easily be worth 5 Merit dots. Which is fine for people that are just crunching numbers, but doesn't work for people that care more about the narrative aspect of the Merit to have to sink half their starting Merit points into it.<br /> <br /> So drawbacks let you balance that out. The mechanical value is decreased, so the cost can be decreased to a level where the narrative value isn't being overridden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:19:13-07:00","id":976508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974845#post974845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole &quot;why have drawbacks&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> The basic design logic is pretty simple. A drawback lets you reduce the cost of a Merit so that it remains accessible. This is important for Merits that have a lot of flavor, but also a lot of potency in concept. If you valued Dual Kith at what it can be effectively worth at the high-mid level of optimization, it could easily be worth 5 Merit dots. Which is fine for people that are just crunching numbers, but doesn't work for people that care more about the narrative aspect of the Merit to have to sink half their starting Merit points into it.<br /> <br /> So drawbacks let you balance that out. The mechanical value is decreased, so the cost can be decreased to a level where the narrative value isn't being overridden.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, what about a 2 and 5 dot version? 2 dot version is as listed, 5 dot version is without drawbacks. If one really wants to, they can pay &quot;full price&quot; to get both fluff and power, while those who just want the narrative impact can play with the cheaper version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:51:45-07:00","id":976581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=974845#post974845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole &amp;quot;why have drawbacks&amp;quot; thing:<br /> <br /> The basic design logic is pretty simple. A drawback lets you reduce the cost of a Merit so that it remains accessible. This is important for Merits that have a lot of flavor, but also a lot of potency in concept. If you valued Dual Kith at what it can be effectively worth at the high-mid level of optimization, it could easily be worth 5 Merit dots. Which is fine for people that are just crunching numbers, but doesn't work for people that care more about the narrative aspect of the Merit to have to sink half their starting Merit points into it.<br /> <br /> So drawbacks let you balance that out. The mechanical value is decreased, so the cost can be decreased to a level where the narrative value isn't being overridden.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its really a win win situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:53:46-07:00","id":976583,"title":"","content":"I'll also point out that with Dual Kith \u2022\u2022 and potent Kith \u2022 you spend as much as you would on the old verison and Potent Kith nullifies the effective penalty to your primary Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:00:19-07:00","id":976590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=976583#post976583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also point out that with Dual Kith \u2022\u2022 and potent Kith \u2022 you spend as much as you would on the old verison and Potent Kith nullifies the effective penalty to your primary Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems legit. You're still at exactly the same drawback as compared to any character that bought Potent Kith without Dual-Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-26-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:11:02-07:00","id":976595,"title":"","content":"I can see you're trying to balance the Merit so that it's not going to be a must-get for every Changeling player. If I get it right, a character with Dual Kith would treat their main Kith as if they had Wyrd - 1 (which can be offset by Potent Kith) while their secondary Kith is treated as having Wyrd - 2? It does work better than allocating your Wyrd dots between the effects of your Kiths. Easier to manage, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T10:48:12-07:00","id":976610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=976590#post976590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems legit. You're still at exactly the same drawback as compared to any character that bought Potent Kith without Dual-Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but my point was that the reduction in price gives you space to also get a dot of potent kith, which midagates the penalty somewhat, that's all. Which is working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:20:23-07:00","id":976625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=976508#post976508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, what about a 2 and 5 dot version? 2 dot version is as listed, 5 dot version is without drawbacks. If one really wants to, they can pay &quot;full price&quot; to get both fluff and power, while those who just want the narrative impact can play with the cheaper version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I see the point. If I wanted to allow this, I'd just let people buy Potent Kith for both Kiths, it's 4 total dots, and you're pretty close. Leaving Potent Kith to fill in that gap allows more flexibility in approach, and doesn't require having two different types of Dual Kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:26:54-07:00","id":976911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=976625#post976625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I see the point. If I wanted to allow this, I'd just let people buy Potent Kith for both Kiths, it's 4 total dots, and you're pretty close. Leaving Potent Kith to fill in that gap allows more flexibility in approach, and doesn't require having two different types of Dual Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm not too concerned about letting people mitigate drawbacks. If they want to do that at their table, they will. But I find dumping points to get rid of a flaw to be a pretty boring thing to spend words on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T06:53:22-07:00","id":977153,"title":"","content":"So the powerbuild now would be to take something that stacks with wyrd for your primary kith, but a not your secondary. Good secondary kiths would be Iles, Ifrit, Mirrorskin, Jeweleyes, etc.<br /> Seeing how Potent Kith won't stack with the second one too, I mean.<br /> <br /> And since buying Dual Kith now is one point cheaper, you can use that one point to buy a point of Potent Kith and Voila. I appreciate the attempt of trying to make it less of a 'must-pick', but I say it's still ridiculously good as opposed to not taking it. The core design of the Merit is just too strong.<br /> <br /> I can't say that I can offer any design choice that will not make it a very good merit, but this is probably a good way to go in an attempt to not make it a MUST-BUY which is more or less was prior to this change.<br /> <br /> Here are some thoughts none the less, of how to design the Merit so it doesn't feel like you'll find yourself building 1 point potent kith and 2 points dual kith every time you intend to take this merit.<br /> <br /> Make it so that picking Dual-kith makes it impossible to take the Potent-kith. Additionally, remove the penalties to your wyrd when calculating the strength of your Kiths. It more or less just encourages you to pick a Kith that doesn't stack with your wyrd either way.<br /> The motivation for not having Dual-kith and Potent kith at the same time could be that using two kiths, the powers of the wyrd won't let you turn one too strong, as it risks consuming the other one.<br /> <br /> Either way, what you did I think is a good attempt at damage control and I am sure that my idea would be littered with exploits too. The very concept of the Merit is just so damn strong in its very core.<br /> Can't wait until the whole thing is out!<br /> <br /> EDIT: I noticed now that you intend to incorporate Wyrd in the kiths that don't have it already. It'll be interesting to see what you conjure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","user":"A_Newfie","date":". 09-27-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T08:10:51-07:00","id":977187,"title":"","content":"I disagree. If people want to focus their power and resources there, there is no good non-Stormwinder reason to not allow it.<br /> <br /> This seems like a good balance point to me, David.I approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:17:40-07:00","id":977291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update#post974244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had a few questions about Dual Kith in 2E. Here's what we're looking at now, different from the original copy I shared:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dual Kith \u2022\u2022</span></span></b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not change.<br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> When taking this Merit, choose one kith as your primary kith. When calculating your kith advantage, your character\u2019s effective Wyrd has one fewer dot, to a minimum of one. The secondary kith\u2019s Wyrd is considered two dots fewer, to a minimum of one as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977153#post977153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the powerbuild now would be to take something that stacks with wyrd for your primary kith, but a not your secondary. Good secondary kiths would be Iles, Ifrit, Mirrorskin, Jeweleyes, etc.<br /> Seeing how Potent Kith won't stack with the second one too, I mean.<br /> <br /> And since buying Dual Kith now is one point cheaper, you can use that one point to buy a point of Potent Kith and Voila. I appreciate the attempt of trying to make it less of a 'must-pick', but I say it's still ridiculously good as opposed to not taking it. The core design of the Merit is just too strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about this alternative to get around all &quot;powerbuild&quot; style of play.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dual Kith \u2022</span></span></b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character\u2019s kith is a unique combination of two different kiths. Whether she\u2019s a flamesiren-windwing who takes the form of a brilliant phoenix, or an elemental who combines airtouched and waterborn in a body of living mist, she benefits from the Blessings of both kiths. If she identifies as one kith, both, or a new kith altogether, the benefits of the Merit do not change.<br /> Taking this Merit after character creation can be as dramatic or casual as desired. The addition of a new kith can be triggered by a change in identity, ideals, goals, even a negative or traumatic event. It\u2019s a meaningful change, but whether or not the change itself stems from a meaningful source is entirely up to the player. The magic the Keepers use to bend body and mind is highly unstable -- who can say what might spark that volatility anew?<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> When calculating things which use Wyrd as a variable in a formula, your character\u2019s effective Wyrd counts as one fewer dot, to a minimum of one, and for purposes of calculating Frailties count your Wyrd as three dots higher, to a maximum of ten.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977299#post977299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's too far to implement downsides/Drawbacks to Kiths? Because then getting both Kith abilities, but both Kith Downsides seems to balance itself out.<br /> <br /> What about an extra Frailty, representing their more unstable nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this solution... edited my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-27-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:30:56-07:00","id":977299,"title":"","content":"I suppose it's too far to implement downsides/Drawbacks to Kiths? Because then getting both Kith abilities, but both Kith Downsides seems to balance itself out.<br /> <br /> What about an extra Frailty, representing their more unstable nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:00:00-07:00","id":977375,"title":"","content":"I don't think we need to add in more drawbacks since David's already said that the main concern that I initially had, and that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6030\" data-vbnamecard=\"6030\">A_Newfie</a> had for that post will be mitigated by ensuring every Kith uses Wyrd in some way; thus eliminating the most glaring of power building issues. +3 effective Wyrd for frailties might work for the &quot;game balance&quot; side of things, but it's a big turn off to the narrative side of things to have to put up with major drawbacks to non-Kith related stuff just to have a Dual Kith that suits your concept really well.<br /> <br /> As well, hitting all Kiths with drawbacks seems unnecessary. Changelings from the preview material have plenty to deal with, and I don't see how adding in more wouldn't have a negative effect of overbearing them with it; esp. not if the biggest reason is to make Dual Kith less &quot;must buy&quot; by virtue of double the drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:10:15-07:00","id":977383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977375#post977375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we need to add in more drawbacks since David's already said that the main concern that I initially had, and that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6030\" data-vbnamecard=\"6030\">A_Newfie</a> had for that post will be mitigated by ensuring every Kith uses Wyrd in some way; thus eliminating the most glaring of power building issues. +3 effective Wyrd for frailties might work for the &quot;game balance&quot; side of things, but it's a big turn off to the narrative side of things to have to put up with major drawbacks to non-Kith related stuff just to have a Dual Kith that suits your concept really well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've always found properly constructed drawbacks add flavor. Tying them to an inherent trait like Kith (since Seeming is now more about the choice that led to the Escape), would be representing that a new form is not all positives - each has strengths and weaknesses. That would be entirely independent of Dual-Kith, and would also make having No Kith have some merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977375#post977375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, hitting all Kiths with drawbacks seems unnecessary. Changelings from the preview material have plenty to deal with, and I don't see how adding in more wouldn't have a negative effect of overbearing them with it; esp. not if the biggest reason is to make Dual Kith less &quot;must buy&quot; by virtue of double the drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it would have been in place of, instead of in addition to the current drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:58:27-07:00","id":977550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977299#post977299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it's too far to implement downsides/Drawbacks to Kiths? Because then getting both Kith abilities, but both Kith Downsides seems to balance itself out.<br /> <br /> What about an extra Frailty, representing their more unstable nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Way, way too late. That'd mean adding over 100 drawbacks. That'd be a pretty intense word count shuffling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:32:16-07:00","id":977749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977550#post977550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way, way too late. That'd mean adding over 100 drawbacks. That'd be a pretty intense word count shuffling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured. Word budgets are such a pain.<br /> <br /> Minor Frailty instead goes too far, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:01:02-07:00","id":978085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=977749#post977749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figured. Word budgets are such a pain.<br /> <br /> Minor Frailty instead goes too far, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I think it might have some unintended consequences. Haven't given it much thought though, since it's this late in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:28:07-07:00","id":978342,"title":"","content":"For potent kith, may I make a suggestion?<br /> <br /> Instead of it only applying to your main kith, have it apply to only one kith, but you can take it multiple times for different kiths. This lets you shore up the penalty if you are willing to dump XP into it, while still lowering the ceiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T08:32:19-07:00","id":978426,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not a big fan of &quot;primary&quot; and &quot;secondary&quot; Kiths, and would prefer the drawback, whatever it may be, apply to both Kiths equally. But, like, it's so late in development, I'm pretty much looking at it as, it'll turn out the way it turns out, and if I need to house rule it I will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:25:49-07:00","id":978499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=978342#post978342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For potent kith, may I make a suggestion?<br /> <br /> Instead of it only applying to your main kith, have it apply to only one kith, but you can take it multiple times for different kiths. This lets you shore up the penalty if you are willing to dump XP into it, while still lowering the ceiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's leaving it open to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:57:08-07:00","id":978655,"title":"","content":"I should have put request, not suggestion. Wrong connotation. Meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:39:30-07:00","id":978948,"title":"","content":"Ehhhh..... is that really a drawback? I mean, sure, there are several kiths out there that scale really well with Wyrd. But there's also a lot of kiths that have nothing to do with Wyrd at all. An Ifrit/Fireheart, lets say. No Wyrd required. <br /> <br /> Aren't we moving in the direction of duel kiths becoming almost necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:21:51-07:00","id":979003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=978948#post978948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhh..... is that really a drawback? I mean, sure, there are several kiths out there that scale really well with Wyrd. But there's also a lot of kiths that have nothing to do with Wyrd at all. An Ifrit/Fireheart, lets say. No Wyrd required.<br /> <br /> Aren't we moving in the direction of duel kiths becoming almost necessary?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been said that Kiths are getting reworked to all interface with Wyrd somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:17:42-07:00","id":979847,"title":"","content":"Ah, I didn't hear that bit'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:12:19-07:00","id":979880,"title":"","content":"Unsurprisingly (and perhaps unavoidably) there's still some powerbuilding based on the full preview of 2e Kiths and Seemings that was just posted, but the gap is now small enough that I don't think it's going to be a serious issue. For example a few Kiths use Wyrd as a dice-pool safety net, that your dice pool cannot fall below. These are probably the best to put as your secondary Kith, because if you plan on being any good at your Kith powers, it's rare that you'll get reduced that much.<br /> <br /> That said, I was going through the official list and the drawback does give a lot of pause if you're looking to select with an eye towards these things. Or at least for most players the amount of fiddling isn't going to be worth it, and the ones that really care aren't going to feel so overpowered for their choice as to be disruptive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:28:07-07:00","id":979889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=979880#post979880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsurprisingly (and perhaps unavoidably) there's still some powerbuilding based on the full preview of 2e Kiths and Seemings that was just posted, but the gap is now small enough that I don't think it's going to be a serious issue. For example a few Kiths use Wyrd as a dice-pool safety net, that your dice pool cannot fall below. These are probably the best to put as your secondary Kith, because if you plan on being any good at your Kith powers, it's rare that you'll get reduced that much.<br /> <br /> That said, I was going through the official list and the drawback does give a lot of pause if you're looking to select with an eye towards these things. Or at least for most players the amount of fiddling isn't going to be worth it, and the ones that really care aren't going to feel so overpowered for their choice as to be disruptive.</div> </div> </div> </div> Whose powerbuilding, I haven't seen that here at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:29:15-07:00","id":979923,"title":"","content":"I certainly do, though more for theory practice than in actual play. It's generally a good idea for at least one person at the table to develop a good eye for what breaks the game and hurts party dynamic so that people don't do it by accident. And if we can make that kind of accidental power discrepancy less likely by giving feedback in open dev, why wouldn't we look for ways to break the system? <br /> <br /> Like, I'm really glad to see the armor kiths got toned down a little, because I have had bad experiences where the survivability difference between armored characters and unarmored characters created huge headaches for the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:39:18-07:00","id":979985,"title":"","content":"Three posters on this thread all spotted the same thing (which was addressed quickly)... so it's something some of us pay attention to. Like HelmsDerp said, it's a useful thing during the open dev because it's another form of the community helping to edit the text before publication, and useful for anything that makes it through (either because nobody caught it, or I as said above the gap is probably acceptable for most groups without causing issues) to know that it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:32:59-08:00","id":1031778,"title":"","content":"As a big fan of hybrid and generalist character concepts, I was very fond of the 1e version of the Merit. As it concerns this one, I do not like the power nerfing, but more importantly I am greatly annoyed by a mandatory distinction between 'primary' and 'secondary' Kiths being forced on the player that wishes to use it. I dearly wish in the end a version of the drawback is made that does not force a such a distinction between the two Kiths. If it does not happen, I am going to houserule it or more simply buy Potent Kith once or thrice in combination with this Merit each and every time I use it to nullify the distinction, xp costs be damned, not so much because I care about the power nerfing (although it is a factor), but mostly because I dislike being forced to pick narrow character niches that much. If I buy Dual Kith, it should be <b>Dual </b>Kith, dammit, not One Kith and Half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-14-2017, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:12:33-08:00","id":1031811,"title":"","content":"You could alway have a three dot version that treats both Kiths as one Wyrd dot Lower instead. That would functionally be pretty much like adding Potent Kith to the secondary one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T22:23:23-08:00","id":1031990,"title":"","content":"Having a distinction between a &quot;primary&quot; and &quot;secondary&quot; Kith isn't an entirely new concept, since the original versions (there were two remember) in 1e had to deal with making sure one Kith was linked to your Seeming even if the other was not. A 1e Dual Kith between a Draconic and a Coldscale had a primary Kith thematically based on if you were a Fairest or a Beast<br /> <br /> As well, the idea that the current version is &quot;One Kith and a Half&quot; is unproductively hyperbolic. The Kith Previews all show that Kiths generally have multiple bonuses and usually only one that relies on Wyrd. As well as one could objectively try to analyze these things, we can see that the drawback is significant without being so potent that one or both Kiths don't fully matter any more.<br /> <br /> As this thread has already well covered, Dual Kith needs a meaningful drawback, or every non-Dual Kith concept is inherently mechanically inferior. Not giving Dual Kith a drawback that makes you think about a fully mechanical Dual Kith, or just refluffing an existing Kith is just &quot;power nerfing&quot; non-Dual Kith characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T23:54:01-08:00","id":1032021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=1031990#post1031990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a distinction between a &quot;primary&quot; and &quot;secondary&quot; Kith isn't an entirely new concept, since the original versions (there were two remember) in 1e had to deal with making sure one Kith was linked to your Seeming even if the other was not. A 1e Dual Kith between a Draconic and a Coldscale had a primary Kith thematically based on if you were a Fairest or a Beast<br /> <br /> As well, the idea that the current version is &quot;One Kith and a Half&quot; is unproductively hyperbolic. The Kith Previews all show that Kiths generally have multiple bonuses and usually only one that relies on Wyrd. As well as one could objectively try to analyze these things, we can see that the drawback is significant without being so potent that one or both Kiths don't fully matter any more.<br /> <br /> As this thread has already well covered, Dual Kith needs a meaningful drawback, or every non-Dual Kith concept is inherently mechanically inferior. Not giving Dual Kith a drawback that makes you think about a fully mechanical Dual Kith, or just refluffing an existing Kith is just &quot;power nerfing&quot; non-Dual Kith characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be content with a drawback that imposes a slght to moderate power price w/o imposing any distinction between the two Kiths, such as Charlaquin's suggestion of a three dot version that treats both Kiths as one Wyrd dot lower. I just loathe being forced to choose a priority between Kiths if I want to break free of such narrow 'class' character concepts. I often like to mix and match character features outside narrow and stereotype thematic archetypes for individual concepts and I usually find CoD games' mandatory choice of 'inborn' splats with serious niche specialization implications (vampire Clans, mage Paths, etc.) terribly constricting and burdensome. E.g. I typically prefer to treat Paths, Clans, Families, etc.as freeform or non-existent as it concerns the choice and development of Arcana, Disciplines, Bans, Atavisms, Lair Traits, and so on. Every hack, Merit, or option that allows to break free somewhat from the prison of mandatory inborn splats is a godsend to me.<br /> <br /> Optimally speaking, I would prefer for the Merit to have two versions, a three-dot version that treats both Kiths as one Wyrd dot lower and a five-dot one that imposes no such price. I acknowledge the differentiation concerns that are driving you to seek a drawback for the Merit, even if I am not sure I can find them that important, since I usually prefer character creation to be strongly freeform. But I think in the version I prefer there would be an adequate balance between making the lesser version of the Merit cheap enough to be widely available for all players interested in hybrid or freeform Kiths, and the greater version pricey enough that only the players really interested in making this a central part of the concept would pick it. Then again, as I said, I can live with only the lesser version existing, if you are concerned that despite the high price too many experienced characters would end up having the greater version (although honestly I don't see much of a problem here). I just want no priority or preference whatsoever between the two Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-15-2017, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T03:31:29-08:00","id":1032066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/974244-dual-kith-update?p=1032021#post1032021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just loathe being forced to choose a priority between Kiths if I want to break free of such narrow 'class' character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the broad context of the paragraph this is in, it doesn't really make much sense. Kiths aren't the in-born splat of the game, they aren't &quot;narrow ' class' character concepts&quot; since almost all of them can be replicated or matched in other fashions. You don't need to be a Venombite to play the &quot;poisoner&quot; niche, it's just a useful free package to a specific mechanical way of embodying that concept. Dual Kith isn't about &quot;breaking free&quot; of this either. Dual Kith is about when you want to go beyond refluffing a Kith to better fit your concept (something the rules already say you can do, if you want a thunderbird instead of a phoenix you can swap electric effects for fire effects instead of Dual Kith electric + fire) and mechanically represent a character that distinctly embodies two different concepts. From the perspective you seem to be coming from, the prioritization should be better, because it creates more character concepts rather than less. The current rules allow there to be more one Kith than the other concepts, where removing the priority means all Dual Kiths are equally both every time. The developer has already said that Potent Kith and Dual Kith aren't going to be written to avoid you taking Potent Kith in your secondary Kith to equalize them, even if that's the intent because some people want that to be an option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I often like to mix and match character features outside narrow and stereotype thematic archetypes for individual concepts and I usually find CoD games' mandatory choice of 'inborn' splats with serious niche specialization implications (vampire Clans, mage Paths, etc.) terribly constricting and burdensome. </div> </div> </div>That's cool. But the rules are written under the assumption that people are using the rest of the rules. If you have more fun changing stuff, change away. But don't advocate for a change to a Merit based on how you like to house rule the core rules of a supernatural splat, because that's just asking for your playstyle to be forced on everyone else. Dual Kith needs to work for people that are using the RAW first, and worry about people house ruling... tenth or something.<br /> <br /> As well, while I appreciate why you feel this way, I also find it a bit silly in a discussion of CtL 2e, which is pretty much the least restrictive CofD to date on this stuff. Not having a Seeming now makes sense as something you might want and is possible to not have, Courts are meant to be custom created for each group rather than picking a set from the books, Kiths are no longer tied to Seemings, and are directly stated to be refluffable, and there's Dual Kith on top of that, etc. The amount of effort the people working on CtL 2e have put in to balance the structure of predefined splats with the desire to facilitate as many player built concepts as possible is astounding, and I don't think Dual Kith's drawback does anything to put more than a microscopic dent in that outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I acknowledge the differentiation concerns that are driving you to seek a drawback for the Merit, even if I am not sure I can find them that important, since I usually prefer character creation to be strongly freeform. </div> </div> </div>How freeform you like your character generation has no impact on the concerns I've raised in this thread, unless free form means completely ignoring all the mechanics character creation choices select for a character. And there comes a point where, &quot;well I don't really care about the mechanics anyway...&quot; turns into, &quot;well then why should we care about your opinions about the mechanics?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}